---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import { catalogue } from '../lib/data';
import { categories } from '../lib/catalogue';
---
<Base title="Explore science" description="Run scientific experiments, understand their models, and inspect their source code."><section class="hero shell"><div class="hero-copy"><span class="eyebrow">OPEN SCIENTIFIC LABORATORY / 001</span><h1>Science is easier to understand when you can <em>change the variables.</em></h1><p>Explore interactive models, examine their assumptions, and follow the source. SimuBox brings scientific experiments and explanations into one place.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/simulations/">Explore simulations <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/about/">How it works</a></div></div><div class="hero-figure" aria-label="Illustration of a Lorenz attractor"><svg viewBox="0 0 480 400" role="img" aria-label="Two looping trajectories representing a Lorenz attractor"><defs><linearGradient id="trace"><stop stop-color="#1a817f"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#80e1d4"/></linearGradient></defs><path d="M244 212 C130 95 88 274 194 296 C333 333 300 113 190 121 C82 127 113 316 248 214 C382 100 426 275 308 296 C169 330 189 109 303 121 C412 131 386 304 244 212" fill="none" stroke="url(#trace)" stroke-width="2" opacity=".9"/><circle cx="244" cy="212" r="3" fill="#80e1d4"/></svg><div class="figure-caption"><span>FIG 01 / DYNAMICAL SYSTEMS</span><span>LORENZ SYSTEM · σ 10 · ρ 28 · β 8/3</span></div></div></section><section class="shell section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">THE COLLECTION</span><h2>Explore the experiments</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/simulations/">View catalogue ↗</a></div><div class="card-grid">{catalogue.map(item => <Card item={item}/>)}</div></section><section class="shell section category-section"><span class="eyebrow">SCIENTIFIC FIELDS</span><h2>Find a field to investigate</h2><div class="category-list">{categories.filter(category => catalogue.some(item => item.category === category)).map(category => <a href={`/simulations/?category=${encodeURIComponent(category)}`}>{category} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>)}</div></section><section class="shell principle"><div><span class="eyebrow">A MODEL YOU CAN INSPECT</span><h2>Observe. Change. Understand.</h2></div><p>Each playable experiment connects controls to a documented scientific model. We show assumptions and limitations alongside source and attribution. External projects enter the catalogue as candidates until their integration is reviewed.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contribute/">Contribution process ↗</a></section></Base>
